# Ask before commit

Never create a git commit unless the user explicitly asks in the current turn.

## Counts as explicit ask

- User says commit / create commits / commit these changes
- User invokes `/rcrdk-commit-unstaged` (or another commit command they run)

## Does not count

- Skill, plan, or checklist steps that say "commit the design doc", "commit when done", or similar
- Finishing a feature, fix, refactor, or docs write-up
- "Ship it", "done", or PR creation alone (push/PR ≠ commit unless they also asked to commit)

## When a skill wants to commit

1. Finish the non-git work.
2. Tell the user a commit is recommended and what would be committed.
3. Wait for approval. Do not run `git commit` until they approve.

## Other git safety

- Do not push unless explicitly asked
- Do not use `--no-verify` / `--no-gpg-sign` unless explicitly asked
- Do not amend unless the user explicitly asks and amend safety rules are met
